        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: George Albert Smith Sr., Wong Jing\n- Organizations: The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints (LDS Church)\n- Places: Salt Lake Valley\n- Monuments: This is the Place Monument\n- Roles: LDS Church president, film director, producer, actor, presenter, screenwriter\n\nFacts:\n- George Albert Smith Sr. was born on April 4, 1870, and died on April 4, 1951.\n- George Albert Smith Sr. was an American religious leader who served as the eighth president of The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints.\n- This is the Place Monument was dedicated by LDS Church President George Albert Smith on July 24, 1947, the hundredth anniversary of the pioneers entering the Salt Lake Valley.\n- Wong Jing was born on May 3, 1955.\n- Wong Jing is a Hong Kong film director, producer, actor, presenter, and screenwriter.",
